      "info": "<div></div>\n<div>\n<h2>🥎 USA Softball North Texas – Region 5 Rec All-Star Championship</h2>\n<p>The <strong>USA Softball Texas Region 5 Rec All-Star Championship</strong> is the premier postseason event for recreational All-Star teams across Texas. This championship brings together top rec players—selected from their local leagues—who have earned the opportunity to compete on a bigger stage.</p>\n<p>Designed to celebrate the spirit of recreational softball, this event delivers a true All-Star experience—featuring competitive play, a high-energy atmosphere, and the opportunity for athletes to represent their teams, leagues, and communities with pride.</p>\n<p>Teams will compete against the best rec All-Star teams from across Region 5 and the state of Texas, with a strong emphasis on <strong>sportsmanship, player development, and unforgettable experiences both on and off the field.</strong></p>\n<hr>\n<h2>⭐ Team Eligibility</h2>\n<p>All-Star teams may be formed in one of the following ways:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A single recreational league All-Star team (players selected from within that league)</li>\n<li>A combined All-Star team made up of players from multiple teams within the same league or community</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This structure allows flexibility while maintaining the integrity of recreational All-Star competition.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>📋 General Information</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Format:</strong> Two (2) pool games seeding into a double-elimination bracket</li>\n<li>Tournament Director reserves the right to adjust format if necessary</li>\n<li>All games governed by <strong>USA Softball Official Rules</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Umpire Fee:</strong> $50 per team, per game (pay at the plate)</li>\n<li><strong>Awards:</strong> Team and individual awards for 1st and 2nd place (top bracket)</li>\n<li>Official game balls will be provided</li>\n<li><strong>Ejections:</strong> Any coach, player, or spectator ejected must sit out the next game</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2>🟦 Pool Play</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Game Length:</strong> 7 innings or 75-minute time limit\n<ul>\n<li>8U &amp; 10U: 65-minute time limit</li>\n<li>Finish the inning</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Games may end in a <strong>tie</strong></li>\n<li>Home team determined by <strong>coin flip</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Run Limit:</strong> 5 runs per inning</li>\n<li><strong>Run Rule:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>10 runs after 3 innings</li>\n<li>8 runs after 4 innings</li>\n<li>6 runs after 5 innings</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2>🟥 Bracket Play</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Teams seeded based on pool play record</li>\n<li><strong>Bracket Format:</strong> Single elimination <em>(unless adjusted by tournament director)</em></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Tie-Breakers (if records are equal):</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Head-to-head results <em>(not applicable if 3+ team tie)</em></li>\n<li>Fewest runs allowed</li>\n<li>Most runs scored</li>\n<li>Coin flip</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Game Length:</strong> 7 innings or 75-minute time limit (finish the inning)</li>\n<li>No ties allowed</li>\n<li>Higher seed = <strong>home team</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Run Limit:</strong> 5 runs per half inning</li>\n<li><strong>Run Rule:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>10 runs after 3 innings</li>\n<li>8 runs after 4 innings</li>\n<li>6 runs after 5 innings</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2>⚠️ Additional Rules</h2>\n<p>Any additions or exceptions to the <span>USA Softball</span> Official Rulebook will be outlined on the event detail page to elevate the level of play while ensuring a competitive and fun experience for all teams.</p>\n</div>",
